{
  "requirement": "Criteria obtain the agent selected by the domain's validation cache through\ntheir `ValidationContext`. The application supplies the configuration under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`. The SDK does not persist it.\nA cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.deterministic_procedures`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The only structural obligation in the text is that criteria obtain the agent selected by the domain's validation cache through their `ValidationContext`. The other clauses describe behavior or only cite other requirements. They are: the application supplies the configuration (a cite of `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`), the SDK does not persist it, and a cache without an agent supports deterministic criteria (a cite of `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.deterministic_procedures`). An alternative that gave criteria a global or separately injected agent would violate the first clause, so that clause is structural.\n\nThe root `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]` meets it. It resolves the agent from `self.ctx.agent`. Otherwise it falls back to `self.ctx.graph.cache().agent`, the `ValidationCache` field in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#struct[ValidationCache]`. That field is `Option<Arc<CachedAgent<D>>>`, and `Default` sets it to `None`. It returns `ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured` when neither is present. So a cache with no agent leaves deterministic criteria unaffected and only fails agent requests.\n\nThe cache's `with_agent` constructor and tool registration belong to `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`. They are not obligations of this requirement text.\n\nbehavioral: Every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent` has a marked test with assertions. I did not read implementation source.\n\n1. **Criteria obtain the cache's agent through `ValidationContext`.**\n   - `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` builds a cache with `ValidationCache::with_agent`. It then verifies a criterion twice. A local transport receives four requests. The test checks the model, the tools and the prompts. The answer is `true`.\n   - `supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat` makes the same kind of check for a second backend.\n   - `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` runs two executions against the supplied agent. It asserts that each execution's usage and dependency trace is its own.\n   - `configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors` checks that a cache with an agent still runs a deterministic question. It also checks that an awaited ask fails with `ValidationError::Provider` and names the missing credential.\n   - `bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted` asserts that `cache().agent` holds the config and that a cloned domain shares the same `Arc`.\n\n2. **The SDK does not persist the configuration.**\n   - The Bedrock test serializes the stored record. It asserts that there is no `backend` key and no profile or model strings.\n   - The OpenAI test stores evidence after each call. It asserts that the saved JSON contains none of `local-transport-key`, `local-test`, `backend` or `api_key`.\n\n3. **A cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria.**\n   - `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` shows that `ValidationContext::ask` returns `NoAgentConfigured`.\n   - The same test verifies a deterministic `Review` criterion, stores its evidence and reloads it with the expected output and dependencies.\n   - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` shows that a missing agent error stores nothing.\n\nThe cited `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent` and `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.deterministic_procedures` are context only. Their tests are not reassessed here.\n\nI found no unmarked relevant test and no untested obligation.",
